<h2>Questions from Williston property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>I own a manufactured home in Williston that was hit by hail. Can appraisal help?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, if your policy includes an appraisal clause and the carrier accepted the claim but you disagree on the amount. Manufactured home roofs, siding and windows often require specific materials, and estimates sometimes miss that.</p></div></details><details><summary>Our apartment complex was built during the boom. Why is matching such an issue?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Boom-era complexes often used one siding and roofing color across many buildings. When products are discontinued, repairing one section can leave a noticeable difference, which is a legitimate question to raise in the claim.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is Williston pricing different from Fargo or Bismarck?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It can be. Labor availability, travel and material delivery affect repair costs in the northwest. We price repairs based on the local market rather than a statewide average.</p></div></details></div>
